gate / any-letter / obligation: confident-wrong over decisions 0.00 (n=240; 95% CI 0.00–0.02) <= 0.02: PASS; Missing an obligation is often unrecoverable — the fine escalates, the hearing passes, the appeal window shuts, and it is held tighter than an invention because the two harms are not equivalent. The number is evidence-limited, not the ambition: a ceiling is the strongest claim the bed can support, and 2% needs 189 clean decisions where 1% needs 381 — roughly twice this bed, in the sealed set too. **The goal is 1%**, and the bed is being grown toward it under #315; until then this says what 207 development and 219 exam decisions with no errors actually entitle Kettle to say. Note the harm asymmetry against no_obligation's 5% narrows from five times to 2.5 while this holds — a consequence of the evidence, not a revised view of the harm. Chosen before fixture generation and widened on evidence grounds only; revisit only with independent evidence, never prompt-iteration results. (2026-08-02)
